f;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Good morning,=
 world. </span><span>The first time I heard K-pop was in 2012. Psy had just=
 had his breakout hit, =E2=80=9CGangnam Style,=E2=80=9D and we were all doi=
ng the horse dance.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,ser=
if;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>K-pop has exploded in popularity in th=
e years since. My kids listen to BTS and watch =E2=80=9CKPop Demon Hunters.=
=E2=80=9D It has put South Korea on the world=E2=80=99s cultural map. But a=
s my colleagues report, there=E2=80=99s also a dark side to all this. I spo=
ke to Sarah Hurtes and Jin Yu Young, who have been investigating the case o=
f the K-pop girl band NewJeans, and their secretive =E2=80=94 some say expl=
oitative =E2=80=94 contracts.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px g=
